  "notes": "Sibling of the 1202SFX with 2 mono and 4 stereo channels (from the panel drawing and the shared controls description). Each mono channel has MIC and LINE IN, but only one can be used at a time. USB audio plays on the last stereo channel (9/10) until a jack is plugged in. The guide contradicts itself on MONITOR OUT (controls: unbalanced; specifications: impedance-balanced TRS). Routing lists where a signal can go; LEVEL, FX and STREAM buttons decide what actually reaches an output. DC power input not listed. Controls from the Quick Start Guide, 'Step 2: Controls' (1-31): mono channels with GAIN, 3-band EQ (+/-15 dB; band names as usual: high, mid, low), LOW CUT, FX send, PAN and LEVEL; stereo channels with FX, BAL, 12 dB BOOST and LEVEL (the LEVEL of the stereo channels follows the panel drawing); FX TO MAIN, PROGRAM (effect preset), STREAM TO MIX and STREAM TO MONITOR (USB and STREAM IN to the main mix / to PHONES and MONITOR OUT), FX TO MONITOR (monitor hears only the FX send), PHANTOM (+48 V on all mono XLR inputs), PHONES/MONITOR level and the MAIN MIX fader (MAIN OUT and STREAM OUT). Modelled: STREAM IN and USB reach the mix or the monitor only with their buttons on; with FX TO MONITOR on, the monitor hears only channels whose FX send is up. Assumptions: the computer records the main mix; levels at MIN are silent; the built-in effect is not modelled as a signal source.",
